// result_begin: markdown
Original rho: Floyd mu 3; lambda 4; entry 3; evaluations 22.
Original rho: Brent mu 3; lambda 4; entry 3; evaluations 17.
Native orbit prefix: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 3, 4, 5, 6].
\image(figures/floyd_graph.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original seven-state successor table has tail states 0, 1, 2 and cycle 3, 4, 5, 6. The colored entry is state 3.)
\alttext(A native directed graph shows zero to one to two to three, then a four-state rectangle three to four to five to six returning to three.)

A fixture table uses storage proportional to its states; the detector's auxiliary
state remains constant. The function can instead compute successors without storing
a table. Instrumentation may count calls, provided the returned successor still
depends only on the state. A callback whose answer changes on repeated equal inputs
does not satisfy the cycle-finding contract.

> Three phases from the actual kernel

In detection, advance the tortoise once and the hare twice before the first equality
test, then repeat. The implementation preserves the original repeated evaluation of
f(x_0): it does not reuse the tortoise's first result for the hare. Thus even a fixed
point takes three detection calls. After a meeting, reset only the tortoise to x_0
without evaluating f; advance both once until they agree, obtaining mu and the entry.
Finally hold the tortoise at that entry and walk the hare once around, obtaining lambda.

The trace records each actual pair before its equality test, including no-call
phase-entry pairs. Orbit indices distinguish equal state labels reached at different
times. They are not counts of unique states: a meeting at indices t and 2t need not
be the entry, and its gap need not be the least period.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_phases.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto next=dm::algorithms::rho_successors(3,4);const auto t=dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(0,[&](auto x){return next.at(x);});
  std::print("| phase | progress | tortoise index | hare index | tortoise state | hare state | completed calls |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::size_t meeting_index=0;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.steps.size();++i){const auto&r=t.steps[i];const auto phase=r.phase==dm::algorithms::CyclePhase::detect?"Detect":r.phase==dm::algorithms::CyclePhase::locate?"Locate":"Measure";
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",phase,r.progress,r.tortoise_index,r.hare_index,r.tortoise,r.hare,r.evaluations);if(r.phase==dm::algorithms::CyclePhase::detect)meeting_index=i;}
  const auto&meet=t.steps[meeting_index];const auto&w=t.work;
  std::print("\nActual phase calls: detection {}; entry recovery {}; period measurement {}; total {}; equality tests {}; recorded pairs {}.\n",w.detection_evaluations,w.entry_evaluations,w.period_evaluations,w.evaluations,w.comparisons,t.steps.size());
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=4;style.height=2.5;style.font_size=23;
  d.node("detect",{0,0},std::format("Meet at state {}\nIndices {} and {}\n{} transition calls",meet.tortoise,meet.tortoise_index,meet.hare_index,w.detection_evaluations),style)
   .node("locate",{5.8,0},std::format("Reset slow to seed\nEntry {} after {} moves\n{} more calls",w.entry,w.result.mu,w.entry_evaluations),style)
   .node("measure",{11.6,0},std::format("Hold entry fixed\nLeast period {}\n{} more calls",w.result.lambda,w.period_evaluations),style)
   .edge("detect","locate").edge("locate","measure").text({5.8,-2.9},"Actual pointer states; recording makes no extra f calls",25).save_svg("build/floyd_phases.svg");
}
