\caption(The original graph meets at state 4 at indices 4 and 8, then recovers entry 3 and measures period 4. Its total is 12 plus 6 plus 4 calls.)
\alttext(Three native nodes show detection at state four after twelve calls, a reset and three lockstep moves costing six calls, and four period-measurement calls.)

> Why the meeting and reset work

Before the tail ends, each tail value occurs only once on the orbit, so x_t cannot
equal a later x_(2t). Within the cycle, equality of those two values means their
index difference t is divisible by lambda. Therefore the first positive meeting
round is

$$
t=\lambda\max\left(1,\left\lceil\frac{\mu}{\lambda}\right\rceil\right).
$$
\alttext(The first meeting round is the period times the larger of one and the ceiling of tail length divided by period.)

Since t is a cycle multiple, the hare at x_(2t) has the same cycle offset as x_t.
Resetting the tortoise to x_0 and advancing both k steps yields x_k and x_(2t+k).
For k less than mu one pointer is in the unique tail; at k=mu both are the entry.
The final walk returns to the fixed entry after exactly the least positive lambda.

For this implementation, each detection round costs three completed calls, each
entry move costs two, and measurement costs lambda. The whole-operation count is

$$
F=3t+2\mu+\lambda.
$$
\alttext(The complete Floyd detector uses three times the meeting round plus twice the tail length plus the period transition evaluations.)

This derivation includes the two recovery phases; it is not just the meeting-search
count. It gives O(mu+lambda) callback invocations and equality tests. Actual runtime
also includes callback cost, integer checks, comparisons and control overhead.

> Preserve the seven quadratic workloads

The original experiment iterates g(x)=(x squared+1) modulo m from seed 2. Each callback
now uses `quadratic_cycle_step`, which evaluates the mathematical polynomial with
widened arithmetic, avoiding uint64 square/add wrap. The seven original moduli are
small enough that their historical expression was already safe, so every answer and
call count remains exact. The native work summaries supply the counts directly.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> x,fc,bc,ratios;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| modulus | mu | lambda | mu+lambda | Floyd detect | Floyd locate | Floyd measure | Floyd total | Brent total | ratio |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::uint64_t m:{1009u,5003u,10007u,50021u,100003u,500009u,1000003u}){
    const dm::algorithms::CycleFunction f=[=](auto value){return dm::algorithms::quadratic_cycle_step(value,m);};const auto a=dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_work(2,f),b=dm::algorithms::brent_cycle_work(2,f);const double ratio=double(a.evaluations)/double(b.evaluations);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.2f} |\n",m,a.result.mu,a.result.lambda,a.result.mu+a.result.lambda,a.detection_evaluations,a.entry_evaluations,a.period_evaluations,a.evaluations,b.evaluations,ratio);
    x.push_back(double(x.size()));fc.push_back(double(a.evaluations));bc.push_back(double(b.evaluations));ratios.push_back(ratio);labels.push_back(std::to_string(m));
    if(a.result.mu!=b.result.mu||a.result.lambda!=b.result.lambda)throw std::runtime_error("quadratic agreement");
  }
  auto counts=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();counts.points(x,fc,"Floyd",{220,38,38},5).points(x,bc,"Brent",{37,99,235},5).x_tick_labels(labels).title("Complete detector calls").xlab("Original modulus (categorical)").ylab("Completed f evaluations").legend({"Floyd","Brent"},{{220,38,38},{37,99,235}});
  auto relative=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();relative.points(x,ratios,"Ratio",{22,163,74},5).x_tick_labels(labels).ylim(1,1.7).title("Observed Floyd / Brent ratio").xlab("Original modulus (categorical)").ylab("Ratio of whole-operation calls");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(counts).add(relative).size(1200,560).title("Original seven deterministic quadratic workloads").fit_panels().save_svg("build/floyd_original.svg");
}
