\caption(Fixed period eight makes the first meeting advance in multiples of eight. Complete detector counts also include recovery; the input fixtures are controlled, not random.)
\alttext(Two native plots show Floyd and Brent callback counts across tail lengths zero to thirty-two and the corresponding Floyd meeting rounds eight, sixteen, twenty-four and thirty-two.)

The ordinary and work APIs retain O(1) auxiliary detector state. The owned Floyd
trace retains O(mu+lambda) actual pairs, with no orbit replay or extra f calls.
The default one-million-row cap is online because the period is unknown in advance.
It checks each next row before its movement or phase reset, including the no-call
locate-entry row. Zero disables only that cap; checked indices and vector limits
remain. An evaluation budget is separate: it can stop between the individual calls
of a tortoise/hare round. No partial trace is returned after either failure.

> Budgets, fixed points, full-width arithmetic and ownership

The original rho needs exactly 22 completed calls and 12 recorded pairs. A limit of
21 calls stops before the twenty-second; a row cap of 11 stops before its last
measurement pair and also leaves 21 calls completed. A successful fixed point still
costs four calls in total: three for detection and one to measure period one.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto next=dm::algorithms::rho_successors(3,4);const dm::algorithms::CycleFunction f=[&](auto value){return next.at(value);};
  bool eval_stop=false,row_stop=false,empty=false,modulus=false;std::size_t eval_calls=0,row_calls=0;
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(0,[&](auto x){++eval_calls;return f(x);},{21},0);}catch(const std::runtime_error&){eval_stop=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(0,[&](auto x){++row_calls;return f(x);},{},11);}catch(const std::length_error&){row_stop=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(0,{});}catch(const std::bad_function_call&){empty=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::quadratic_cycle_step(2,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){modulus=true;}
  const auto complete=dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(0,f,{22},12);
  std::print("Exact admission: completed calls {}; actual pairs {}; mu {}; lambda {}.\n",complete.work.evaluations,complete.steps.size(),complete.work.result.mu,complete.work.result.lambda);
  std::print("Evaluation budget21 stopped {}; completed calls {}; row cap11 stopped {}; completed calls {}.\n",eval_stop,eval_calls,row_stop,row_calls);
  std::print("Empty callback rejected {}; zero modulus rejected {}.\n",empty,modulus);
  const auto fixed=dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(42,[](auto x){return x;});std::print("Fixed point42: mu {}; lambda {}; calls {}; pairs {}.\n",fixed.work.result.mu,fixed.work.result.lambda,fixed.work.evaluations,fixed.steps.size());
  const auto full=std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();const auto residue=dm::algorithms::quadratic_cycle_step(full,full-58,full);
  std::print("Full-width polynomial: state {}; constant {}; modulus {}; residue {}.\n",full,full,full-58,residue);
  auto mutable_next=next;const auto owned=dm::algorithms::floyd_cycle_trace(0,[&](auto x){return mutable_next.at(x);});mutable_next.clear();std::print("After caller table cleared: owned entry {}; final pair {} / {}.\n",owned.work.entry,owned.steps.back().tortoise,owned.steps.back().hare);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=4.5;style.height=2.6;style.font_size=24;
  d.node("exact",{0,0},std::format("Successful trace\n{} calls; {} pairs\nmu {}; lambda {}",complete.work.evaluations,complete.steps.size(),complete.work.result.mu,complete.work.result.lambda),style)
   .node("calls",{6.2,0},std::format("Evaluation limit 21\n{} calls completed\nNo returned trace",eval_calls),style)
   .node("rows",{12.4,0},std::format("Online row cap 11\n{} calls completed\nNo returned trace",row_calls),style)
   .text({6.2,-3},"Budgets do not undo completed callback effects",25).save_svg("build/floyd_controls.svg");
  if(!eval_stop||!row_stop||!empty||!modulus||eval_calls!=21||row_calls!=21||fixed.work.evaluations!=4)throw std::runtime_error("checked cycle controls");
}
